// ===========================================================================
// 6. Scalar math and fixed-layout copy helpers (`0x802A0830..0x802A89D0`)
// ===========================================================================
//
// These are small leaf functions from the same GX render band. None of their
// own bodies contains a paired-single instruction (`fn_802a0830` merely calls
// a GQR helper); the float work is plain `lfs`/`fmuls` or plain `stfs`, and
// the copies move whole words so bit patterns survive. They are used by the
// vertex/material paths above but are independent of this module's FIFO code.

/// Packs `(a, b)` through the opaque matrix helper into `dst` and returns it.
///
/// The callee is called as `0x801C0540(a, b, dst)`; it returns `dst` in `r3`,
/// but the original reloads `r3` from its saved `dst` anyway, so this wrapper
/// also returns `dst`.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_802A0830` at `0x802A0830` (60 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/802a0830_FUN_802a0830.c`
/// - Raw check: `work/dol/main.elf` at `0x802A0830..0x802A086C`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `dst` - destination operand (`r3`), forwarded as the third callee
///   argument.
/// * `a` - first source (`r4`), forwarded as the first callee argument.
/// * `b` - second source (`r5`), forwarded as the second callee argument.
///
/// # Returns
/// `dst`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Whatever `0x801C0540` writes through `dst`; the wrapper itself only saves
/// and restores `r31`/`LR`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `a`, `b` and `dst` must satisfy the matrix helper's requirements. The
/// helper's body is paired-single/GQR code and stays opaque here.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high for the argument shuffle and return value; medium for calling the
/// helper "matrix-shaped" (its Ghidra C is a GQR mis-render).
pub unsafe fn fn_802a0830(dst: usize, a: usize, b: usize) -> usize {
    // observed 0x802A0844..0x802A0850: r3=a, r4=b, r5=dst, then bl.
    call3(FN_801C0540, a as u32, b as u32, dst as u32);
    dst
}

/// Copies three consecutive floats.
