/// Clamps a `[0, 1]` scalar and maps it to a 16-bit table value.
///
/// Below `0.1356144` the function returns the floor value `80`; from `0.9`
/// upwards it returns `16000`. In between it indexes the `u16` table at
/// `0x802FCC00` with `(int)((value - 0.1356144) / 0.03333334)`, i.e. a
/// 30-step ramp between the two stored limits.
