/// Writes five 16-bit fields of the record selected by a clamped index.
///
/// The index is clamped with the sign-mask idiom: negatives become 0 (the
/// `& ~(x >> 31)` arm) and anything from `0x80` up becomes `0x7F`. The record
/// is ten bytes wide at `0x802FC700` and holds five `u16` values; they are
/// written to the five output pointers in order.
