/// Appends up to `length` halfwords to the ring buffer at `+0xD8`.
///
/// The usable capacity is `(u16[+0xFC] >> 1) - 1` when that word is non-zero;
/// the write is clamped to `capacity - start`, the write cursor at `+0xFE` is
/// updated, and the slot after the last written entry is zeroed.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_802AEFA0` at `0x802AEFA0` (196 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/802aefa0_FUN_802aefa0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `object` - ring-buffer owner (`r3`).
/// * `source` - halfword source (`r4`).
/// * `start` - first destination index (`r5`).
/// * `length` - maximum number of halfwords (`r6`).
///
/// # Returns
/// The number of halfwords copied, or zero when there is no buffer or no room.
///
/// # Side effects
/// A block copy, the cursor store at `+0xFE`, and one zero halfword.
///
/// # Safety
/// `object` must own a buffer at `+0xD8`; `source` must be readable for
/// `length * 2` bytes.
