// primary vtable (`0x802FE3D8` at `0x80006CEC`, `0x803294C0` at `0x8016390C`),
// `this + 0x10` is built by `0x802ACB40` (which installs the *base* vtable
// `0x8034F878`) and is then re-vtabled to `0x803294D8`, and `this + 0x30` is
// built by `0x802B4D30`. So `0x803294D8` is the **secondary vtable of the
// `+0x10` member object**, installed at `member + 0x00`.
//
// **Relation to `0x8034F878`.** The base vtable `0x8034F878` (14 slots, header
// `0x8034F878`, methods `0x8034F880..0x8034F8B8`) holds the same 14 words except
// for two: slot 0 is `0x802ACB80` (base destructor) instead of `0x80006D90`
// (deleting destructor) and slot 3 is `0x802AD080` instead of `0x801634D0`.
// That is exactly the override pattern of a derived class whose remaining 12
// methods are inherited verbatim - the identity evidence for the "derived"
// reading.
//
// **Identity.** The member is the layout root of the class the `0x802FE3D8` /
// `0x803294C0` constructors build. Slot 1 validates an `RLYT` header (magic at
// `+0x00`, byte-order mark `0xFEFF` at `+0x04`, version at `+0x06`) and then
// walks the section list at `resource + u16[+0x0C]`, dispatching on the
